---
import { profile } from "~/data/profile";
import Prose from "~/layouts/Prose.astro";
---

<Prose
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What akshaygujjula.com collects, why, and how to have it removed."
  dateline="Last updated 23 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    This is my personal website. I'm {profile.fullName}, based in London, and I'm responsible for
    any personal data it handles. You can reach me at
    <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    There are no analytics, no advertising and no tracking on this site. The only personal data I
    receive is what you type into the contact form.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you send a message, your name, email address and message are delivered to my inbox through
    Cloudflare Email Routing. They are not stored in a database on this site. I use them only to
    reply to you, and I delete the conversation when you ask me to. The legal basis is my
    legitimate interest in answering messages people choose to send me.
  </p>

  <h2>Spam protection</h2>
  <p>
    The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people apart from bots. It loads only when
    you scroll to the form, and it processes technical signals from your browser to make that
    decision. Cloudflare describes what it collects in the
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile privacy addendum</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare hosts the site. Like any web host it processes technical information such as your IP
    address to deliver pages and protect against abuse, as set out in
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage on your device</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies of its own and stores nothing in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK data protection law you can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data I hold
    about you, or object to how I use it. Email me and I'll respond within a month. If you're
    unhappy with how I've handled your data, you can complain to the
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. The full history is public in the
    <a href="https://github.com/AkshayReddyGujjula/AkshayReddyGujjula">site's repository</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
